// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; T27F-007 task card whose inner metrics come from the semantic tokens of vf_tokens (Refs gHashTag/t27#13214, epic #13214)
; Layering, fixed by the brief: the scene supplies semantic objects, vf_tokens supplies the numbers, vf_layout owns the geometry,
;   vf_card (vc_render_m) draws what the layout resolved. This module is the seam between the first two and the third: it reads eleven tokens,
;   builds the same card as stories/task_card.t27 with those numbers in its padding and gap fields, and edits none of vf_tokens, vf_proportion,
;   vf_layout, vf_pixel or the story. It is not a second token system and holds no scale of its own
; The eleven tokens, by name (vtk_find then vtk_resolve; a status other than VTK_OK refuses and no value is guessed):
;   space.card.padding 16, space.field.label_gap 6, space.field.group_gap 16, space.action.gap 10,
;   type.heading 26, type.label 16, type.body 16, layout.card.max_inline 560, control.min_target 24, border.width 1, space.control.inset 6
; vct_metrics: VctMetrics, status 0 only when all eleven resolve. On any other status every number is 0 and vct_graph_with returns a blank graph
; vct_card_graph(width): card{title, badge, field{owner-label, owner-input}, actions{save PRIMARY, cancel SECONDARY}}, 9 nodes
;   card: column, padding = space.card.padding, gap = space.field.group_gap. field: a column stack, gap = space.field.label_gap
;   actions: a row stack, gap = space.action.gap. Texts and variants are those of task_card_graph. viewport_w = width
; Expected rects (the card is 230 high at every width, only the card width follows the viewport):
;   0 card 0,0 / 1 title 16,16 80x20 / 2 badge 16,52 48x24 / 3 field 16,92 160x66 / 4 label 16,92 80x20 / 5 input 16,118 160x40 /
;   6 actions 16,174 202x40 / 7 save 16,174 96x40 / 8 cancel 122,174 96x40
; Narrow cards (was KNOWN limitation 1, closed by the step 03 layout rule): vf_layout now holds a child to the inner cross extent of its parent,
;   so the card keeps its padding at any width. Below 234 px the actions row is held to width - 2 * 16 and its buttons give way; below 192 px the
;   input is held too. At 320 and 280 nothing narrows. The test pins both sides of the edge
; Long labels (KNOWN limitation 2, narrowed): vf_layout itself still measures no text. A text node is 80 x 20 whatever it says, so a label
;   such as "Responsible owner of this task" is wider than its node at type.label 16 px (vf_type measures it) when this module's plain layout is
;   used. The caller that measures is vf_card_fit (vf_layout_m with the vf_type widths); the test here pins the plain-layout fact
; Seam fact, held by a test: the vf_theme defaults TH_CARD_INSET (16) and TH_CARD_MAX_W (560) equal space.card.padding and layout.card.max_inline
;   (they were 12 and 480 before the reconciliation), so vc_render and vc_render_state draw the same inset and width as the token style. A change of
;   a token or of a theme constant alone fails vct_theme_defaults_equal_the_tokens
; All arithmetic is u32 and non-negative: compare before subtracting. ASCII only (L3)

